  "S3": {
    "bottom_line_reference": "Using the oracle assumptions and filed base-year figures, the DCF yields a base-case equity value of about 226 per share. A +/-50 bp WACC band gives a fair-value range of roughly 205 to 252 per share. Against the oracle market price of 286.12, that implies the shares screen overvalued on this cash-flow setup. The valuation is highly terminal-driven, with about four-fifths of EV coming from terminal value, so robustness to terminal assumptions is limited. The EV-to-equity bridge matters materially because net debt is large; dividing EV directly by shares is the wrong basis. This conclusion is conditional on the oracle margin, reinvestment, tax, and WACC inputs rather than any company-published discount rate. Cross-checking cyclicality, leverage, capex normalization, and market multiples remains important.",
